N64: declare 48 kHz so the frontend does not resample

Pairs with 0002. With the core producing 48000 natively and the codec
running at 48000, declaring it here means RetroArch performs no rate
conversion at all.

Signed-off-by: RetroBPI_M2M

--- a/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -884,7 +884,9 @@
    info->geometry.max_height   = screen_height;
    info->geometry.aspect_ratio = 4.0 / 3.0;
    info->timing.fps = (region == SYSTEM_PAL) ? 50.0 : (60.13);                /* TODO: Actual timing  */
-   info->timing.sample_rate = 44100.0;
+   /* RetroBPI: 48000 to match the codec exactly, so the frontend performs no
+    * rate conversion at all. The core now resamples straight to this rate. */
+   info->timing.sample_rate = 48000.0;
 }
 
 unsigned retro_get_region (void)
